= Teacher Answer Key

*Section A:* 1 (b); 2 (d); 3 (b); 4 (c); 5 (c)

*Section B:* 1) 2, 1, 2  2) 1, 5, 3, 4  3) 2, 6, 2, 3  4) 1, 3, 2, 3  5) 1, 3, 2

*Section C:*
- 6(a) $10.0 / 22.99 = 0.435$ mol Na
- 6(b) NaCl moles = 0.435 mol (1:1 ratio with Na); mass $= 0.435 times 58.44 = 25.4$ g
- 6(c) Cl₂ moles = $0.435 / 2 = 0.2175$ mol; mass $= 0.2175 times 70.90 = 15.4$ g
- 7(a) $5.00 / 44.10 = 0.113$ mol C₃H₈
- 7(b) CO₂ moles $= 3 times 0.1134 = 0.340$ mol; mass $= 0.3401 times 44.01 = 15.0$ g
- 7(c) O₂ moles $= 5 times 0.1134 = 0.567$ mol; mass $= 0.5669 times 32.00 = 18.1$ g

*Section D:*
- 8(a) Mg moles $= 2.43 / 24.31 = 0.100$ mol. Mg needs $2 times 0.100 = 0.200$ mol HCl but only 0.150 mol is available, so HCl is limiting.
- 8(b) H₂ moles = half of HCl moles $= 0.075$ mol; mass $= 0.075 times 2.02 = 0.151$ g
- 8(c) Mg consumed $= 0.075$ mol; remaining $= 0.025$ mol; mass $= 0.025 times 24.31 = 0.608$ g

*Section E:*
- 9(a) Theoretical yield = 25.4 g
- 9(b) $22.1 / 25.4 times 100 = 87.0%$
- 9(c) Examples: incomplete reaction, product lost during transfer or filtration, impure reactants, side reactions.

